tuyalan-sim (a simulated Tuya LAN device, in Go)
Copyright 2026 Abhinav Gautam

This module is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE).

The code was written for SigmaM2M, a oneM2M platform, from public
descriptions of the Tuya LAN protocol (PROVENANCE.md). It contains no
code from other projects. sim/sim.go comes from SigmaM2M and carries no
per-file copyright header, the convention of the code it comes from; the
copyright line above covers it. Files added for this module carry
"Copyright 2026 Abhinav Gautam" and "SPDX-License-Identifier:
Apache-2.0".

Trademarks
----------

Tuya is a trademark of its owner. This module is not made, endorsed or
supported by Tuya, and is not affiliated with it; the name is used only
to say which devices it simulates.

Facts from other projects
-------------------------

The protocol facts come from public descriptions, chiefly tinytuya
(github.com/jasonacox/tinytuya; MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 Jason Cox),
through the tuyalan module. No code was taken.

Interop tests (interop/, a separate test-only module)
-----------------------------------------------------

interop/peer/Dockerfile installs tinytuya 1.20.0 (MIT, Copyright (c)
2024 Jason Cox) and its dependencies from PyPI into a
python:3.12.10-slim image at test time (v0.1.0 ran on python:3.14-slim);
nothing of tinytuya is copied into this repository.
interop/peer/client.py is our own script that calls tinytuya.

Dependencies
------------

- github.com/cB-Sigma/tuyalan (the Tuya LAN protocol; Copyright 2026
  Abhinav Gautam, Apache-2.0, standard library only).
- The Go standard library (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright The Go Authors).

Test data
---------

Every device ID, local key, product key and address in this module is a
made-up demo value.
